Let an embedder keep ssh out of debug mode.

SSHMaster passes `-v` to ssh when nix::verbosity is CHATTY or more, and
ssh writes its debug lines to the inherited descriptor 2. No logger sees
them, so a log tap or a subscription cannot keep them off stderr.

huggorm pins nix::verbosity at CHATTY, so every ssh-ng store it opened
ran ssh with `-v`: one `solid sbom` against a remote build store wrote
about 200 `debug1:` lines to stderr (nixidae/nixidae#1390).

ssh's level is a remote connection's level, the one `remoteVerbosity`
already holds for a daemon. Below zero, the default, it is
nix::verbosity, so `nix -vvvvv` still gets `ssh -v`.

Needs the remote-verbosity patch of the same lane.

--- a/src/libstore/ssh.cc
+++ b/src/libstore/ssh.cc
@@ -5,9 +5,16 @@
 #include "nix/util/util.hh"
 #include "nix/util/exec.hh"
 #include "nix/util/base-n.hh"
+#include "nix/store/remote-store.hh"
 
 namespace nix {
 
+static bool sshVerbose()
+{
+    auto level = remoteVerbosity.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    return (level < 0 ? verbosity : (Verbosity) level) >= lvlChatty;
+}
+
 static std::string parsePublicHostKey(std::string_view host, std::string_view sshPublicHostKey)
 {
     try {
@@ -197,7 +204,7 @@
